<.shell current={:confirm_dialog}>
  <h1>Confirm dialog</h1>
  <p class="lead">A question before a change that can't be undone.</p>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>Before a delete or a send that can't be undone.</p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>A change that can be undone, or one the person reviews on the page first.</p>

  <h2 id="simple">Simple</h2>
  <p>
    Most deletes and sends. The question names the thing; the sentences after it say what happens.
    The action button names the action: red for a delete, blue otherwise.
  </p>
  <div class="demo grid gap-6">
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-delete"
      open
      question="Delete the endorsement First Aid?"
      body="It comes off ID cards and out of Callout's rules."
      action="Delete endorsement"
      variant={:danger}
    />
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-send"
      open
      question="Send 22 changes to D4H?"
      body="Members who arrived are marked attended with their times. 3 who signed up and didn't arrive are marked absent."
      action="Send changes"
    />
    <div>
      <.button
        id="confirm-try-simple"
        variant={:danger}
        data-confirm="Delete the endorsement First Aid? It comes off ID cards and out of Callout's rules."
        data-confirm-button="Delete endorsement"
      >
        Delete endorsement
      </.button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>A better way out</h3>
  <p>
    A third button when there's a better way out than going ahead, such as a link to fix the cause. At most one red button.
  </p>
  <div class="demo grid gap-6">
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-alt"
      open
      question="Retire Sam Lee?"
      body="They still hold 2 items: Radio 14 and Helmet 3. D4H won't retire a member who holds equipment."
      alt="Open their equipment"
      alt_href="#simple"
      action="Retire when returned"
      variant={:default}
    />
    <div>
      <.button
        id="confirm-try-alt"
        data-confirm="Retire Sam Lee? They still hold 2 items: Radio 14 and Helmet 3. D4H won't retire a member who holds equipment."
        data-confirm-button="Retire when returned"
        data-confirm-alt="Open their equipment"
        data-confirm-alt-href="#simple"
      >
        Retire
      </.button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="check-box">Check box</h2>
  <p>
    Only where a delete takes other things with it: a group with members, an activity with
    attendance, a qualification someone holds. The dialog lists what's lost and ends with
    "D4H can't bring it back." The action stays grey until the box is ticked.
  </p>
  <div class="demo grid gap-6">
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-check"
      open
      question="Delete the group MIT 2026?"
      list={[
        "14 members leave it.",
        "Its 2 rules are deleted.",
        "Rope Rescue Callout's rules name it, and stop until you fix them."
      ]}
      warning="D4H can't bring it back."
      check="I understand 14 members and its rules are lost."
      action="Delete group"
      variant={:danger}
    />
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-checked"
      open
      question="Delete the group MIT 2026?"
      list={[
        "14 members leave it.",
        "Its 2 rules are deleted.",
        "Rope Rescue Callout's rules name it, and stop until you fix them."
      ]}
      warning="D4H can't bring it back."
      check="I understand 14 members and its rules are lost."
      checked
      action="Delete group"
      variant={:danger}
    />
    <div>
      <.button
        id="confirm-try-check"
        variant={:danger}
        data-confirm="Delete the group MIT 2026?"
        data-confirm-list={Jason.encode!(["14 members leave it.", "Its 2 rules are deleted."])}
        data-confirm-warning="D4H can't bring it back."
        data-confirm-check="I understand 14 members and its rules are lost."
        data-confirm-button="Delete group"
      >
        Delete group
      </.button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="type-to-confirm">Type to confirm</h2>
  <p>
    Built, and used nowhere yet. Only for something that wipes a team's data. The action
    turns on once the text matches, ignoring case and spaces, with no error while typing.
  </p>
  <div class="demo grid gap-6">
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-type"
      open
      question="Delete Coast Range SAR from SAR Duty?"
      body="Its tax credit letters, scans, chores, check-ins, and group rules are deleted. Nothing in D4H changes."
      warning="SAR Duty can't bring it back."
      type="Coast Range SAR"
      type_label="Type the team's name to confirm"
      typed="Coast Ra"
      action="Delete team"
      variant={:danger}
    />
    <.confirm_dialog
      id="confirm-example-typed"
      open
      question="Delete Coast Range SAR from SAR Duty?"
      body="Its tax credit letters, scans, chores, check-ins, and group rules are deleted. Nothing in D4H changes."
      warning="SAR Duty can't bring it back."
      type="Coast Range SAR"
      type_label="Type the team's name to confirm"
      typed="coast range sar"
      action="Delete team"
      variant={:danger}
    />
    <div>
      <.button
        id="confirm-try-type"
        variant={:danger}
        data-confirm="Delete Coast Range SAR from SAR Duty? Its tax credit letters, scans, chores, check-ins, and group rules are deleted. Nothing in D4H changes."
        data-confirm-warning="SAR Duty can't bring it back."
        data-confirm-type="Coast Range SAR"
        data-confirm-type-label="Type the team's name to confirm"
        data-confirm-button="Delete team"
      >
        Delete team
      </.button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Cancel has the focus, so Enter by reflex does nothing. Escape cancels.</li>
    <li>On a phone the buttons stack full width, the action on top.</li>
    <li>
      It is our own dialog, not the browser's: some phone browsers never show <code>window.confirm</code>, so the button did nothing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>data-confirm="…"</code>
    on the button, with <code>data-confirm-button</code>
    naming the action. A check box adds <code>data-confirm-list</code>, <code>data-confirm-warning</code>, and <code>data-confirm-check</code>; type to confirm adds
    <code>data-confirm-type</code>
    and <code>data-confirm-type-label</code>; a better way out adds <code>data-confirm-alt</code>
    and <code>data-confirm-alt-href</code>. The root layout renders
    <code>&lt;.confirm_dialog /&gt;</code>
    once, and <code>assets/js/confirm_dialog.js</code>
    fills it in and opens it.
  </p>
</.shell>
